urlmon: keep the "res" scheme out of the empty-host URLZONE_INVALID rule

MapUrlToZone() feeds WPF's MS.Internal.SecurityHelper.MapUrlToZoneWrapper, which throws
SecurityException("The URI specified is invalid.") whenever the returned zone is negative.
AutoCAD 2027's WPF control dictionaries reference images as
"res:///%25prodname%25btn.xmx/$10/$RCDATA_16_COLOR"; Windows 11 26200 maps that URL to
URLZONE_INTERNET (3), while Wine's get_zone_from_domains() special-cases every hierarchical
scheme - including the Wine-only URL_SCHEME_RES - that has an empty host to URLZONE_INVALID.
Every dictionary containing such an image then fails to load: the ribbon loses its control
styles and RibbonContent.mRibbonControls stays empty, so AcMgdStatusBar's status-bar item
lookups raise the modal ".NET Assertion Failed - Failed to get status bar item with key
AcSb*" dialog and the UI stops painting.

Windows only applies the "hierarchical scheme needs a host" rule to the schemes it really
treats as hierarchical, so excluding URL_SCHEME_RES lets the URL fall through to the
ProtocolDefaults lookup, which defaults to URLZONE_INTERNET exactly like Windows.

Measured with tools/zonetest on both OSes (same binary, .NET 10.0.9):
  res:///%25prodname%25btn.xmx/$10/$RCDATA_16_COLOR   Windows 3   Wine 0xffffffff -> 3 (patched)
  res://acadbtn.xmx/$10/$RCDATA_16_COLOR              Windows 3   Wine 3
  pack://application:,,,/AcWindows;component/...      Windows 3   Wine 3
--- a/dlls/urlmon/sec_mgr.c
+++ b/dlls/urlmon/sec_mgr.c
@@ -450,6 +450,7 @@
      * assigns URLZONE_INVALID to the zone.
      */
     if((scheme_type != URL_SCHEME_UNKNOWN && scheme_type != URL_SCHEME_FILE)
+        && scheme_type != URL_SCHEME_RES
         && is_hierarchical_scheme(scheme_type) && !*host) {
         *zone = URLZONE_INVALID;
 
